WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.522
A nanomolar potency value can win a meeting before

00:00:04.522 --> 00:00:08.142
anyone asks whether the compound reaches the relevant

00:00:08.142 --> 00:00:09.047
tissue unbound.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.840
A compound works at nanomolar concentration in a

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.653
protected assay. The number is seductive, but a patient

00:00:22.653 --> 00:00:24.772
never receives an assay plate.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.496
Solubility, absorption, distribution, metabolism and

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:39.152
clearance decide whether the required free

00:00:39.152 --> 00:00:41.589
concentration reaches the tissue.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.879
A high tissue or plasma concentration can conceal

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:54.737
extensive binding. Free exposure at the site of action

00:00:54.737 --> 00:00:56.452
is the relevant question.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.779
Ask what dose achieves occupancy for long enough, and

00:01:06.779 --> 00:01:10.108
what happens elsewhere in the body at that same

00:01:10.108 --> 00:01:10.478
exposure.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.943
Target affinity, binding in biological matrices and

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:25.436
pharmacokinetics must be reconciled with the exposure

00:01:25.436 --> 00:01:27.432
needed for an effect.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.627
Potency cannot compensate indefinitely for permeability

00:01:36.627 --> 00:01:40.108
barriers, toxicity or infeasible pharmacokinetics.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.687
The assay number matters only if it can be translated

00:01:50.687 --> 00:01:52.805
into a defensible exposure strategy.
